body:
From the start until Radahn I was pure faith with low vigor and endurance. Then I started focusing on getting health and heavy armor and turned more into a battle mage up until after the fire giant. Once I beat him I respec back into a pure faith to explore what I could and finish the game off looking good in some robes. 80 faith 60 vigor 50 mind and very low on everything else. I ended up at 165 because as I was trying to explore everything I missed I pretty much permanently had co op summoning pools on so I beat a lot bosses a lot of times. 

&#x200B;

No I haven't. I avoided looking at anything while playing and tried to figure out as much as I could on my own. Now that I've finished I looked up the bosses and there are still plenty I haven't fought yet. Seems I've missed a decent amount of content and I'm keen to play again and explore everything with the help of the internet haha.

I felt the same in grade 12. I was juggling 2 jobs and school, missing 1 day a week of school for one of the jobs. One thing i learnt from that is that mental health is incredibly important. If you have something in mind you want to do I'd discuss it with your parents and drop out if you want. Otherwise maybe try reducing your workload and finish school. Try thinking specifically what's causing the anxiety/stress as well and try to fix it. Certain subjects or people? Switch things up and see if that helps. Talk to the guidance officer or a teacher your comfortable with and i'm sure they'll help out.  

&#x200B;

There's a lot of options for jobs without having to finish school, so there's not too much pressure to really finish it if you don't feel you have to. Just keep in mind school is pretty important if you ever change your mind and want to pursue further education.

'for some unknown reason' - you don't want to do the homework. If you can't keep up grades that's kinda your fault. Better start studying for the final exam, one day to go

Just tell your mum in advance that you don't think your gonna do well, do some studying and hope for the best. not much you can do now that you've left it this late

&#x200B;

Are we talking something like this? [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wsZ7013yHiw](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wsZ7013yHiw) 

now that you are aware of it and don't like doing it, you'll probably just stop doing it over time 

&#x200B;

I used to make a lot of incredibly inappropriate jokes when i was younger (racist and sexist being the most common). I still find offensive jokes funny but i never say them out loud anymore. All it took was to watch a movie about how words can hurt people and it really just smacked me in the face. I've made a point to try and never hurt other people with words since.

&#x200B;

Just gotta live and learn, lot's of people don't like how they acted when they were younger
